\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 FRANK FIGLIUZZI, MSNBC NATIONAL SECURITY CONTRIBUTOR: So first, you`re right, if you review the charging documents, written by prosecutors in the January 6 thcases, over and over and over again, you`ll see references to social media. Either posting plans beforehand, posting activity during or bragging about it afterwards. And there`s a role there that`s been played, and it`s significant.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And you`re going to see it come forward in the trials of these people charged for January 6th. Now, why isn`t Facebook completely owning up to it? Well, look, first, it`s ugly stuff, if they say we helped do this really bad thing, they better have a way to fix it. And I don`t believe they do yet because it`s highly complicated. And of course, the bottom line comes into play. It`s about profit. One of the solutions would have to be somehow decoupling the profit incentive from these algorithms that keep people driving down into these rabbit holes.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It`s as if you booked an excursion to climb a rock. A rock climbing excursion with an experienced guide and you fell down and you almost had disaster with injury. And the next time you book that rock climbing excursion, they say, you know what, the last time you were here, you fell down, and you got hurt. And I think you must really like that. So we`re going to get you another excursion and we`re going to ensure that you fall down and get hurt.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 That`s what happens in the rabbit holes on Facebook algorithms. You went here, we`re going to give you more of that. And there`s not enough effort to say it`s dangerous. It`s violent. It`s a debunked conspiracy theory, and it leads to really bad things happening. They haven`t figured out how to do that and still make money.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: I -- yes, I mean, I believe they figured it out. They just choose curtain number two, that`s a personal opinion. I`m going to read their statement on this topic specifically. They might regret that I do this, but I`m going to read this. This is from Facebook. The growth of people or advertisers using Facebook means nothing if our services aren`t being used in ways that bring people closer together.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 That`s why we`re investing so much in security that impacts our bottom line. Protecting our community is more important than maximizing our profits to say we turn a blind eye to feedback ignores these investments, including the 40,000 people working on safety and security at Facebook. And our investment of $13 billion. So Claire, the problem with that is, you know, don`t cry for me, Argentina, it costs us a lot of money.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But here`s their mission statement. Here`s the problem. We want to make sure that our services aren`t being used that -- in ways that bring people closer together. They brought them so close together that hundreds of them seeking to hang Mike Pence descended on the U.S. Capitol. I -- this is a personal opinion. I think Facebook is the most maligned force in this country. Other than crimes, criminal enterprises, drug deals, drug dealers, gangs, are obviously more maligned than Facebook.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But other things that aren`t illegal or criminal, I think Facebook is the most damaging influence in this country and to say, we balanced, you know, the bottom line with keeping our people together is absolute hogwash. Do you think they`ll be eaten up on Capitol Hill or do you think this is still a blind spot?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 CLAIRE MCCASKILL, MSNBC POLITICAL ANALYST: Well, first of all, it`s back the truck up a little bit. Congress, when the internet began decided they were going to make it the Wild West, there was going to be literally no regulation and in fact, went so far as to give all of these sites immunity from anything bad that is posted on their sites. Now fast forward, the internet has been an amazing economic engine in this country.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But what these -- all these sites figured out is that they track you, they know what you want to buy, and that monetize it. And for Facebook, and other sites, if you`re afraid or you`re angry, you`re going to hang out more. And there`s no editors. This isn`t like traditional media where things are fact checked by editors. And when you pick up the daily paper, The Washington Post or the St. Louis Post-Dispatch, you know, somebody is checking to make sure the information is correct.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It will be the Wild West until Congress steps up. Because Facebook going away, Nicolle, you don`t think there`s going to be another one that fills that space in a nanosecond. There`ll be another company that will come right behind it doing the same thing because that`s the environment we`ve created on the internet, to reward fear and anger. So I say to the members of Congress, quit stalling, get busy and regulate these companies.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 [16:10:09]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Yes. I mean, Miles Taylor, I want to play more from the whistleblower on this specific point up there -- they know how good they are at disseminating hate.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I`m going to read it actually. From Facebook`s internal research, how can secretly copied a study this year that said, in part, according to 60 Minutes, we estimate that we may action as little as three to five percent of hate and about 0.6 percent of violence and incitement on Facebook, despite being the best in the world at it. What an alarming claim to fame. And I wonder from your sort of existence, that the Department of Homeland Security and sort of having part of that responsibility of monitoring extremism here at home, how prevalent you think Facebook is?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 MILES TAYLOR, FORMER CHIEF OF STAFF, HOMELAND SECURITY DEPARTMENT: Well, I`ll tell you, not just that, Nicolle, but after I left DHS, I actually went and worked in big tech for a while I worked at Google. And it was fun, it was adult Disneyland, you get free snacks, the tech sector is a great place to work. But what I saw in the broader industry, is that there was a willful blindness to the damage that a lot of platforms were doing out there to our democracy.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And Facebook was front and center on that. I mean, I thought of Facebook as the nightmare, if you will, of social division, and have public safety concerns and of national security threats. So when I was at DHS, we flew out to the west coast, probably once a quarter to go meet with these tech companies to talk about abuse of their platforms by terrorists, by nation states, like Russia that were engaging in foreign interference.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And it`s not that they didn`t want to do anything about it. It`s just that they were exceptionally excruciatingly slow and doing anything because, as you noted at the top, and these were platforms built to make connections between people not to keep them from connecting. That`s great when it`s you reconnecting with your nieces and your aunts and uncles. It`s not great when you`re helping child predators can act or worst, or equally as bad insurrectionists at the U.S. Capitol.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So I think what`s really worrying here is there`s clear damning evidence, this whistleblower brought the receipts, she`s showing that Facebook really tried to cover up these mistakes. And I can`t break news on this today. But I can tell you this, Mark Zuckerberg has got more to worry about because I think there`s going to be a waterfall of whistleblowers following this one. There are others out there who feel the same way and I suspect that we`re going to hear from them in the days to come.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Are you working with some of them? How do you know that, Miles?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260
\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 TAYLOR: I can`t answer that directly. But I knew a lot of folks that worked and currently work in that company. And I think Zuckerberg should be sweating that this is not something that just one person at Facebook bell, I think there are other people who felt the same way who may be looking to be out there as well.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Let me -- let me pick the scab one more -- one more time, if you can`t answer I understand. Was the insurrection and Facebook`s role in housing. Some of the content that -- as I said, is now mentioned in some of the court filings that are making their way through the Justice Department criminal investigation. Was that a factor as far as you understand and people reaching a point where they may want to speak out?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 TAYLOR: Yes. Look, I think so. I mean, I think there are folks going all the way as far back as before the 2016 election who, you know, I think in that time period, you really started to see more Facebookers expressing concerns about how the platform was being manipulated for political purposes. I certainly had that worrying government. I mean, in 2016, is I`ve seen how Facebook, let its algorithms be hijacked by foreign nation states to influence the outcome of an election.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 People forget, Brad Parscale, you know, who later became Trump`s campaign manager went out. And he gave a major public hat tip to Facebook. And I don`t have the exact quote, but I think he said something like, they`re one of the key reasons we won this election. And that`s because they allowed the campaign to do questionable things to target voters. And of course, as we know, they allowed foreign nation states to manipulate their platform which affected our democracy.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So I think there`s more going to come out about that. And I think there`s a lot of disaffected Facebookers who`ve left the company for those reasons.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Frank, from a law enforcement perspective, I mean, look, I think there are multiple reasons why Facebook runs free, as Claire said, is true, like the Wild West. One is with all due respect to Claire and I would carve her out of this sweeping generalization. There`s not a lot of sort of savvy tech folks in the Senate and -- or in the House. But the other is that tech companies can screen out content.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I mean, I think Google took down terrorist instruction manuals I believe multiple platforms have taken down. They have a screen for child pornography. They know exactly. How to remove offensive content. I don`t think this is a tech problem. I think this is a problem of will.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 [16:15:05]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: And I think because it was one of the two political parties in this country associated with domestic violent extremism that they, you know, sort of stood back. But I wonder if you think that`s changed. Now that you have Christopher Wray testifying for almost a year straight, that right-wing domestic violent extremism is the single greatest threat facing this country. Do you think that calculation shifts?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 FIGLIUZZZI: I do know that as bad as all this sounds it -- to reference something that Claire said earlier, this could be a whole lot worse if someone else were to come in behind Facebook. So they`ve got anywhere between 20,000 and 40,000 employees who come to work every day at Facebook, under the rubric of safety and security. They do report the low hanging fruit, the easy child exploitation filter, the violent talk, I`m going to - - I`m going to hurt this person.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The plans to kidnap somebody. That goes right to law enforcement. They`ve got a neat way of doing that. They could do a whole lot more, but I keep coming down to profit. They haven`t figured out how to do it. You know, journalism one on one, if it bleeds, it leads the old -- the old adage about headlines and titles and front pages of newspapers and T.V. shows. It`s a modern day version of that.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 People want negativity. They want to be panicked, afraid, they`re coming after my kids, they`re coming after Christmas, right? And they keep going down those rabbit holes. And we`ve got to kind of decouple that from getting ad revenue. And they haven`t done that yet. I want to -- I want to say a couple of things about bringing people together at Facebook, I`ve got stories, and these are -- these become public stories by the way.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Al Qaeda, people coming together because they simply got caught in an algorithm on Facebook where they were watching the same beheading videos and violent sermons. And the Facebook algorithm say, hey, you guys are watching the same stuff. Would you like to be friends, and you`re essentially creating terrorist cells on Facebook. They`ve gotten much better at that. But it`s nowhere near where it needs to be.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 If we`re going to start stopping down on the violence that`s coming from people going down the rabbit hole of misinformation and disinformation and propaganda. At one point, during the 2016 presidential election, a quarter million people were following fake Facebook accounts established by the Russian government.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Claire, Frank said something so important, and I think is a good place to turn this, you know, if it bleeds, it leads. It`s a tenant of local news. Tragically, people probably feel that that has some relevance on cable news. And that`s fair, but we can`t put anything on the air that isn`t true, or we`re subject to litigation. We have to -- newspapers and newspaper reporters have to live by libel laws. We live by slander laws. Why shouldn`t Facebook Live by the same laws?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 MCCASKILL: That`s a really good question. And, you know, the interesting thing is that because you referenced it earlier. I mean, there was a famous hearing, Nicolle, where the Republican -- where the chairman of the committee that had jurisdiction over the internet, actually talked about the internet as a series of tubes. I remember -- I remember famously a chairman of the same committee that I served on at one point, saying to a witness who had a screenshot up on a projector saying, would you fax that to me?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So, we have a real problem with the ability of Congress to keep up with the rapidity of the development of the internet and the tech that goes with it. I don`t know how many members of Congress really understand the algorithms that if my nephew starts we`ll see Joe Rogan, all of a sudden he is sucked in to this void, this black space with all that misinformation. I don`t know if they know how to do it but they need to get busy and do it.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Libel and slander need to apply they need to remove 230 or change it significantly. So there`s not this blanket immunity, which never would go into effect now. If it had to start from scratch. A blanket immunity for all these companies for anything that appears on their sites.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: And I guess, Miles, what`s so exasperating is now we know, OK, at the beginning of Facebook, maybe we just thought grandmas would share pictures of their grandkids and their walks. But that`s not how -- now we know, now we know better. Now we know they disseminate dangerous disinformation about politics. Now we know they disseminate dangerous information about masks.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Now we know. Why can`t we as a country fix things that turn out differently than then we hope because we`re different than we thought?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha
\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 TAYLOR: Yes, I think it`s a big challenge you faced with these -- with these companies. I mean, we know the problems real. There`s a lot of reticence to address it, but I also want to address something that the Senator just said about Section 230 because the companies will come back at those arguments for reform. And they will say, well, if the responsibility is on the people who use the platform, we create a place for them to communicate.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We have to hold individuals accountable if they, you know, push for violence or engage. And to an extent that that`s, you know, to an extent that that`s true, you know, I agree. But one of the problems with that is that these companies also go egregiously slow in providing that information to law enforcement. I mean, there are local police departments, and Frank knows this all around the country who put in subpoenas, civil subpoenas, for requests for Instagram accounts or Facebook accounts associated with individuals who are, you know, holding people hostage with nude photos or committed other criminal acts.}
