\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So, I hope that he does -- I hope that he -- this is a sign of an increased amount of emotion and passion from this administration and from our surrogates, quite frankly, across the country to push this agenda.}{
\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2
\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Claire, I want to know what you think and I also -- you know, I don`t think it`s a clear-cut political win for Republicans to be on the side of shutting down the government. How do you see this?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24
\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0
\ulnone\cf2 MCCASKILL: Well, first of all, it`s much worse than shutting down the government. It is -- shutting down the government is something that`s kind of inside Washington baseball where who`s going to get laid off? Who is not going to get paid? How long will it be before they get their backpay?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This is different. And here`s what Mitch McConnell is betting on. He`s betting that most Americans will never understand that this is about paying the bills for money that`s already been spent. He`s counting on them, not understanding because it sounds like you`re raising the limit on your credit cards, you could spend more, he`s counting on Americans to not know who to blame and not really understand that this is just about being good to our word. This is about American not being a deadbeat.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 So, what has to happen here is Joe Biden has to talk about this around the clock. Chuck Schumer has to talk about it, all the democratic senators have to talk about it. What Mitch McConnell is doing is in fact, politically crazy, if Americans know what he`s actually doing. He`s counting on the fact that they won`t understand it.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: It`s an amazingly important point, Claire McCaskill. We`re going to put you on the hook. We`re coming back and staying on this. Because I think he`s also counting on it being this, sort of, inside conversation that`s happening along all this other messy stuff, so you make -- you make perfect points, both of you.}
