\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: That was called the State Warriors coach, Steve Kerr, telling reporters that yesterday that hesitant NBA star, Andrew Wiggins, has been vaccinated against COVID, and now, he meets California`s vaccine mandate for large indoor events that would have barred him from playing home games if he hadn`t. Adding to the league`s impressive 95 percent player vaccination rate.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It comes as the New York Times` David Leonhardt writes about the virus in retreat once again, citing the steady pace of vaccinations nationally, cases, hospitalizations, deaths, all consistently down for weeks along with natural immunity, even higher this time around, for better or for worse. All of it he says puts the, quote, worst of the pandemic almost certainly behind us.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Leonhard write says, "Eventually, immunity will become widespread enough that another wave as large and damaging as the Delta wave will not be possible. Barring something unexpected. Dr. Scott Gottlieb told me. I`m of the opinion that this is the last major wave of infection."}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Joining our conversation MSNBC medical contributor, Dr. Vin Gupta. He is a pulmonologist and a global health policy expert. Do you agree? Are we done?}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 VIN GUPTA, MSNBC MEDICAL CONTRIBUTOR: Good afternoon, Nicolle. I think we are over certainly past the worst of the fourth surge. Do I think we`re done when it comes to losing 1,500 Americans day over day for the next several weeks? No. So, I think it depends on what our definition of done is. We`re still expecting an additional 100,000 Americans dead by the beginning of the new year, that number could be worse based on what plays out over the course of the next few months.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We`re entering cold and flu season. So, there`s many threats over the next four to five months. We have to be vigilant regarding flu, respiratory syncytial virus. So, there`s a lot of things here that we need to still remain vigilant on.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: I want to put up the vaccine data. We spent a lot of time on the vaccine hesitant and then the straight up anti-vaxxers, but this feels like a number we`re celebrating, 77.6 percent of all eligible adults in the U.S. have received at least one dose. Is the number still 85 percent that folks feel like we need to reach or have the infections been so vast and so tragic and so sweeping that we may be inching towards something that 77 percent is a good number?}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 [16:55:10]}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 GUPTA: You know, I think 77 percent is a good number in every ZIP code, Nicolle. The problem here is in parts of Florida, you still have 20 percent of the most vulnerable, not vaccinated, which is why Florida ICUs are full.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I was just in Tennessee shipping patients that were critically ill over 65 to Cleveland for advanced ICU care. So, it depends on the demographics of the ZIP code. So that number is great, but it would be great if it was in every single zip code, 75 percent or higher.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 WALLACE: Tell me where folks like yourself who have, sort of, seen around some of the corners think we`re heading the rest of this year and into the beginning of next.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 GUPTA: You know, there was data that came out over the weekend, Nicolle, suggesting that this virus is even more airborne that we thought it was back in February of 2020 when President Trump first heard about it. What does that mean? That means that when you cough, and if you have COVID, you release a large -- lot of large mucus balls, large droplets and some small ones, airborne droplets that travel far distances.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 What does that mean? That means that if you`re unvaccinated, and even for the vaccinated who are high risk, we should be talking about better masking. Number one, especially now as we`re thinking about mandating vaccines for large employers, if those employers choose not to implement the vaccine, or a vaccine mandate, what do we -- what do we do with the unvaccinated? We test them weekly, but maybe they should be wearing better masks. That`s number one.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 But to your point directly, Nicolle, all the threats that are out there, as a pulmonologist, I`m worried about our health system, not only dealing with the high plateau of COVID daily deaths, a 1,000 to 1,500 well into January, that`s a lot. In addition, we`re dealing with all the other things out there, elective procedures, flu, all the other threats. That`s what concerns us.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
